## Quick Start

### 1. Install Dependencies

```bash
# Install pkg dependencies
cd pkg
go mod tidy

# Install app dependencies
cd ../apps/{{.AppName}}
{{- if not .UseLocalFramework}}
go get github.com/KOMKZ/go-yogan-framework@latest
{{- end}}
go mod tidy
```

### 2. Run Application

```bash
cd apps/{{.AppName}}

# Show help
go run main.go --help

# Run home command
go run main.go home

# Run home info
go run main.go home info

# Run home ping
go run main.go home ping
```

### 3. Build

```bash
# From project root
make build-all

# Or build specific app
make build APP={{.AppName}}
```

## Adding New Commands

1. Create command file in `apps/{{.AppName}}/internal/command/`:

```go
package command

func RegisterXxxCommands(root *cobra.Command, app *application.CLIApplication) {
    xxxCmd := &cobra.Command{
        Use:   "xxx",
        Short: "Description",
        Run: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {
            // Implementation
        },
    }
    root.AddCommand(xxxCmd)
}
```

2. Register in `apps/{{.AppName}}/internal/app/commands.go`:

```go
command.RegisterXxxCommands(c.rootCmd, core)
```

## Adding New Domains

```bash
mkdir -p domains/my-domain
cd domains/my-domain
go mod init {{.ProjectModule}}/domains/my-domain
```

Then add to `go.work`:

```go
use ./domains/my-domain
```
